**Commentary of al-Shinqiti (Adwa' al-Bayan) on surah 33, verse 63:**

His saying, exalted is He: ﴿They ask you, [O Muhammad], about the Hour. Say, "Its knowledge is only with Allah."﴾ In this noble verse, Allah the Exalted commanded His Prophet (ﷺ) to say to the people who ask him about the Hour: ﴿Its knowledge is only with Allah﴾. It is known that *innama* (only) is a particle of *hasr* (restriction or exclusivity).

So the meaning of the verse is that no one knows the Hour except Allah alone.

This meaning, which this noble verse indicates, is made clear in other verses of the Book of Allah, such as His saying, exalted is He: ﴿Indeed, Allah has knowledge of the Hour and sends down the rain﴾ [Luqman: 34], up to the end of the verse.

The Prophet (ﷺ) also explained that the five matters mentioned in His saying, ﴿Indeed, Allah has knowledge of the Hour﴾, up to the end of the verse, are what is intended:

• by His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And with Him are the keys of the unseen; none knows them except Him﴾ [al-An'am: 59];

• and by His saying, exalted is He: ﴿They ask you about the Hour: when is its arrival? Say, "Its knowledge is only with my Lord. None will reveal it at its time except Him. It has become heavy [a burden] upon the heavens and the earth. It will not come to you except suddenly." They ask you as if you were well informed about it. Say, "Its knowledge is only with Allah, but most of the people do not know"﴾ [al-A'raf: 187];

• and by His saying, exalted is He: ﴿They ask you about the Hour: when is its arrival?﴾ ﴿In what [position] are you to mention it?﴾ ﴿To your Lord is its finality﴾ [al-Nazi'at: 42–44];

• and by His saying, exalted is He: ﴿To Him is referred the knowledge of the Hour﴾, up to the end of the verse [Fussilat: 47]. And in the hadith: "The one asked about it is no more knowledgeable than the one asking."

His saying: ﴿And what would make you know? Perhaps the Hour is near﴾. In this noble verse, Allah, majestic and exalted, mentioned that the Hour, which is the Resurrection, may be near. He mentioned something similar in His saying in al-Shura: ﴿And what would make you know? Perhaps the Hour is near﴾ [al-Shura: 17]. Allah, majestic and exalted, has also clarified its nearness in other verses:

• such as His saying: ﴿The Hour has drawn near﴾, up to the end of the verse [al-Qamar: 1];

• and His saying: ﴿The time of their reckoning has approached for the people, while they are heedless and turning away﴾ [al-Anbiya': 1];

• and His saying, exalted is He: ﴿The command of Allah has come, so do not seek to hasten it﴾, up to the end of the verse [al-Nahl: 1].
